  "scope": "Managed authenticated original non-commit and independently approved alternate account-root targets; same native registry/enrollment/journal engine.",
  "behavior": [
    "Closed original plans retain old-root suspension and exact original parent ownership, with or without a bound freeze.",
    "The next target comes from independently retained approval; original non-commit and next freeze are separately authenticated.",
    "Registry closure, next preparation and exact binding precede original parent/child reconciliation.",
    "Unknown results repeat the exact transition, including an initial unfenced parent, existing history or already completed target. Missing files are not recreated.",
    "Multiple abandoned targets keep original operation IDs and select the final account at revision 2 exactly once.",
    "A known closed next target is refused before mutation; old retry cannot select it again.",
    "Receipt decoding/signature/requested-scope failures preserve the controller and unrelated application authority. Persistence/recovery failures retain the consume-and-reconcile contract."
  ],
